    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d397">

                <pb facs="0887" n="791" sameAs="frus:frus1945Malta/pg791"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Hopkins Papers</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The President’s Special Assistant</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hopkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the President
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Yalta</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-02-08">February 8, 1945</date>.]<anchor n="1"
                            xml:id="d397-f1"/>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. President</hi>:—The Joint Chiefs of Staff told
                        Welles<anchor n="2" xml:id="d397-f2"/> that it would be difficult for us to
                    defend their coasts against Japan. That is Welles excuse.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harry</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d397-f1" n="1" xml:id="d397-f1-content">
                <p>This note is undated but is assumed to have been passed to the President at the
                    plenary session on February 8 in connection with the President’s reference to
                    Welles and the reasons why certain South American states had not declared war.
                    See <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg773">p. 773</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d397-f2" n="2" xml:id="d397-f2-content">
                <p>The Department of Defense states that there is no evidence in the files of the
                    Joint Chiefs of Staff to substantiate this statement.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
